WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.750
There’s one formula in this module, and it’s worth more points than anything else you’ll learn here.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.650
Look at the screen.

3
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:11.575
Sixty times distance, equals speed times time.

4
00:00:11.825 --> 00:00:14.250
Distance in nautical miles.

5
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.250
Speed in knots.

6
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.125
Time in minutes.

7
00:00:18.375 --> 00:00:20.875
Remember it as sixty D street.

8
00:00:21.125 --> 00:00:23.025
Sixty, D, S, T.

9
00:00:23.275 --> 00:00:26.600
From that one line, you can find any of the three.

10
00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:30.625
Time is sixty times distance, divided by speed.

11
00:00:30.875 --> 00:00:34.725
Distance is speed times time, divided by sixty.

12
00:00:34.975 --> 00:00:38.750
Speed is sixty times distance, divided by time.

13
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.800
Try the example.

14
00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:43.350
Twelve miles, at eight knots.

15
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.150
How long?

16
00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:49.425
Sixty times twelve is seven hundred twenty.

17
00:00:49.675 --> 00:00:52.400
Divided by eight is ninety minutes.

18
00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:54.600
One thing to notice.

19
00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:57.825
The answer comes out in minutes, not hours.

20
00:00:58.075 --> 00:01:00.775
That’s the whole reason the sixty is there.
